ancer and ovarian cancer) and is annotated as one contiguous Composite Mention before the clinical head cases.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 2 - Composite Mention\"},{\"start\":986,\"end\":1003,\"text\":\"hereditary cancer\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"Hereditary cancer refers to a family of multiple specific cancers defined by inheritance, so it is a Disease Class; the term cancer is retained.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What NOT to Annotate 4 - General terms (cancer retained); What to Annotate 1 - Disease Class\"},{\"start\":1438,\"end\":1462,\"text\":\"hereditary breast cancer\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"Hereditary breast cancer refers to a class of multiple specific hereditary breast cancers in the population, so it is a Disease Class.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1 - Specific Disease / Disease Class\"},{\"start\":1598,\"end\":1622,\"text\":\"hereditary breast cancer\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"Hereditary breast cancer refers to a family of multiple specific hereditary breast cancers after the quantifier some proportion of, so it is a Disease Class.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1 - Specific Disease / Disease Class\"}]}", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 9719, "output_tokens": 14762, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 13405}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}